In order to implement the 20 major decisions of the Good Party in a spirit of striving to implement them, firmly advance Chinese modernization, lift up your sleeves and refuel your body like a construction captain, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
It is important to remember that from the ruling party, the self-revolution of the party will always be on the way, and from the political responsibility of the ruling party, the political construction of the party will be dominated, and the new great project of building the new era of the party will be profoundly promoted.
Strengthen the promotion of high-quality leadership development, the leadership of the masses in service, the prevention of disintegration of risk leadership, the intensification of research, the firm prevention and overcoming of formalism and bureaucracy.
The ceremony was attended by Shitaipeng, Li Kangje, Li Shukyu, Chen Cheng, Wang Xia Hong, and Chen Shi presided over the ceremony.
Vietnamese Prime Minister Van Minh and the couple's official visits to Singapore and Brunei have been successful and have achieved comprehensive, pragmatic and concrete results.
During his three-day visit to Singapore and Brunei, Prime Minister Van Ming took part in more than 30 different events.
The results obtained have given new impetus to the continuous development of the new bilateral strategic partnership and the Vietnamese comprehensive partnership in a deeper, broader and more effective direction.
During his visit to the two countries, the Prime Minister continued to reaffirm the outward course of the Vietnamese Party and the country, which is independent, autonomous, diverse, multicultural, willing to be good friends and reliable partners of all countries, and responsible members of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei are the needs of their respective countries, committed to enhancing the well-being of their peoples, and committed to regional and global peace, stability and development.
At meetings and negotiations, Prime Minister Van Minh and the leaders of Singapore and Brunei unanimously agreed to continue strengthening political mutual trust with Vietnam through high-level delegation visits, effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during the visit.
Among them, the Memorandum of Understanding on the Green and Digital Economic Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening the Comprehensive Vietnamese Partnership signed with Brunei for the period 2023-2027 are two highlights.
Vietnam signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the Green Paper and Digital Economic Partnership with Singapore.
Image from Vietnamese news agency
During meetings with business leaders, talks or attending economic forums, Prime Minister Van Ming emphasized Vietnam's welcome and facilitated conditions for Singaporean and Brunei businesses to expand their investment in areas such as digital transformation, green energy, high-technology, innovation and innovation in Vietnam.
This visit will not only contribute to deepening Vietnam's cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in the traditional fields of politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education, training, oil and gas, tourism, and civil exchange, but also create a framework for cooperation between countries in new potential areas such as the digital economy, green economy, energy transformation, innovation, smart cities, and sustainable development.
King Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei is preparing for a bilateral meeting with Prime Minister Van Ming.
Image from Vietnamese news agency
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Van Minh also set aside time to visit and listen to the thoughts and wishes of the local Vietnamese community.
During the meeting of the leaders of the two countries, Prime Minister Van Ming suggested that the authorities of the two countries pay more attention and that the local Vietnamese community be treated fairly, with opportunities to contribute to local society and to foster the relationship between the two countries.
The proposal was approved and supported by the leaders of both countries.
In particular, the Prime Minister also shared with the leaders of the two countries the desire for an ASEAN Community of unity, peace, stability and prosperity; unanimously agreed to maintain cooperation in solidarity with ASEAN countries and enhance ASEAN's central role in the complex and changing context of regional and international situations.
With the significant achievements achieved, Prime Minister Van Minh's official visit to Singapore and Brunei has been instrumental in the effective implementation of the 13th Foreign Route as a priority for strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbours, in the effective implementation of the 12th Conclusion of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of Vietnam (CPC) on the new situation in Vietnam, and in contributing positively to the strengthening of national unity.
(Finished)
What exactly was the meteor shower that was shot down over Alaska?
They have gone astray and conjectured.
The U.S. military on Friday afternoon (February 10) again used America's most advanced stealth jet F-22 to shoot down an unidentified object flying over the U.S. state of Alaska.
The site of the crash is 10 miles off the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time the U.S. military has shot down a flying object in less than a week.
On Saturday, a spy balloon from China was shot down off the coast of South Carolina, USA, days after floating over US airspace.
The Pentagon said the second object to be shot down entered U.S. airspace for the first time on Thursday night and was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska, flying at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), about the size of a small car and much smaller than the Chinese spy balloon that was shot down earlier.
The Pentagon also believes that there is currently no indication that the object is manoeuvrable.
White House National Security Council Strategic Communications Coordinator John Coby said on Friday that while the exact appearance of the object in high-altitude flight is unclear, it poses a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aviation aircraft.
Kobe said the object was unlike the spy balloon found in the United States, which did not have a payload suspended above it.
Coby said, "Well, we call it a clay object clay, and that's the best description we've been able to come up with at the moment".
President Biden listened to the Pentagon's suggestions before ordering the shooting down of the object, and he made the decision very carefully, Kobe added.
The official U.S. description of the object can be roughly summarized as: the size of a small car, no handlebars, no suspension devices, and a flight altitude of about 10,000 meters.
However, this information still fails to answer basic questions such as what the object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Many online analyses and speculations suggest that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may have come from China, as did the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that flew over Latin America, which performed some task in different locations.
It has also been linked to a UFO sighting in Alaska.
U.S. Newsweek reported citing former U.S. Representative Peter Meijer's tweet on Friday, "I really hope that the UFO bomb is also a spy balloon, not a legitimate UFO bomb".
It's surprisingly ironic that Liu confused alien spacecraft with weather balloons, but that's not worthy of triggering an interstellar conflict, Meijer said.
Meager tweeted this shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
According to Newsweek, the object is suspected of being a UFO by more than one Major.
Rep. Tim Burchett, a Republican from Tennessee, criticized the government's cover-up of intelligence last month, asking the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) to release a report on the unidentified flying saucer.
Iran commemorates the anniversary of the revolution, hackers supporting the protests hijack the president's televised speech
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official rally on Saturday to commemorate the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ibrahim Lacy's televised address.
The president's live TV talk on the Internet was interrupted for about a minute when a sign appeared on the screen of a group of anti-Iranian government hackers, whose names are Adalat Ali ((Ali Justice) ️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️️
There was also a voice screaming for the death of the Islamic Republic.
According to Reuters today, on the anniversary of the Iranian revolution, hackers disrupted state television.
As Iran officially commemorates the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, Lacey's hardline government faces the toughest challenge of the young protesters demanding their resignation, but Lacey still calls on the deceived youths to repent so they can be pardoned by Iran's supreme leader.
Nationwide protests continued in Iran after 22-year-old Amini Mahsa Amini died in the custody of the country's moral police in September.
The deadly crackdown on the protests by Iranian security forces was one of the biggest challenges facing the Islamic Republic since the 1979 revolution toppled the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty commemorating the Revolutionary Anniversary, Iranian authorities on Friday released imprisoned dissidents Farhad Mesami and Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelha from hunger strike protests.
Earlier, Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty order, including some of the prisoners arrested during the recent anti-government protests.
According to human rights organization HRANA, as of Friday, 528 protesters have been killed, including 71 minors.
According to reports, 70 other government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for a vote at Saturday's rallies to express opposition to the protests and support for the government.
On Friday night, on the eve of the anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, the official media showed fireworks as part of a government-sponsored celebration, and people chanted "Allahu Akbar!"
(God is the greatest!)
However, in the rallies, many people can be heard shouting that the dictator is dead!
In a video posted on social media, the footage of the Islamic Republic of Iran was captured.
On Saturday, government television broadcast live videos of official state gatherings across the country.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebration, national anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lacey's speeches are often interrupted by the slogan "dead in the United States" - an iconic slogan in state assemblies.
The crowd also shouted that Israel should die.
According to Reuters, Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 on national security charges.
She was subsequently placed under house arrest, but returned to prison in January.
Adelkhah denied the allegations.
A week before his release, supporters warned that he was in danger of dying as a result of hunger protests.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the forced wearing of a headscarf.
The French Foreign Ministry on Friday responded to Adelkhah's release and called for her freedom to be restored, including allowing her to return to France if she wished.
