Finally gathered together, the Crown Jewels, what we are talking about when we talk about love.
I think that this collection of novels, as well as its title, is like an art of behaviour, and the author wants to express that love is more than just mourning on the stage, the sea of ruins in urban legends, not only that you make me feel like paint, love is more than that and shouldn't be represented above, love is also life as flat as water, as dry as day to day, as well as the restlessness of life, the escape from reality, the uncertainty of the future.
When you read this book, you may think of the couple who fought alongside you, the tasteless marriages of those you knew, and the unpleasant feelings you felt.
That's why I don't recommend reading, because from an aesthetic point of view, the writing and the plot of the book are invaluable, unless your life is as surprising or as sweet as living in a candy castle, and you have to feel weird and boring when you read it.
From the depths of thought, the daily scenes do not brighten the eyes or expand one's thoughts and visions (which is different from Marx's love affair of the Cholera Period) and the short clips do not explore any issues, such as what mistakes led to the failure of love?
What is the reason for the breakdown of the main marriages?
So I don't recommend reading this book, because reading or not reading doesn't make much sense.
The author's thoughts are expressed more in terms of technique and body language than in terms of storytelling, which is also the reason for the poor reading experience of the book.
